# Publish-without-rebuild routing for /deliverable/* and /sla/* is handled
# by Pages Functions (functions/deliverable/[[path]].ts and
# functions/sla/[[path]].ts), not by rules here. A _redirects wildcard was
# tried first and rejected after empirical testing against a deployed
# preview: Cloudflare applies _redirects rules unconditionally regardless
# of whether a static file exists at the request path, and a same-path
# "passthrough" rule (source === destination) turned out to be a silent
# no-op rather than a working exclusion — it never took precedence over a
# wildcard listed after it. Functions give real conditional logic instead
# of relying on that text DSL's undocumented edge cases, and Functions
# already take precedence over static assets by default, so no _redirects
# entry is needed for these paths at all.
